{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"contact@atkn.me","session":"kandev:21960baf-2813-4805-9ab8-21feb414f91c","created_at":"2026-08-26T02:20:00Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"A pull request head can be based on an older commit than the current base tip, so treating the base tip as the predecessor causes receive validation to recheck unrelated history and confuses review-base evidence with transition ancestry.","decision":"Use the PR merge-base as the continuity predecessor while retaining the current base commit tree as the evidence binding; compare evidence base trees to that explicit binding.","impact":"Non-rebased pull requests validate only their proposed transition, while a changed review base invalidates evidence through the base-tree binding instead of producing unrelated-history obligations.","recurrence_control":"The receive fixture covers base-tree invalidation, and the GitHub adapter derives the merge-base for pull_request proposals before invoking the shared checker.","alternatives":["Compare review evidence only to the contributor branch predecessor","Force every pull request branch to rebase before receive validation"],"sources":[{"relation":"implements","kind":"issue","ref":"github:phynics/reveries#3"}],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
